IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je54-nouns`
IMPORT `je54-vintage`
IMPORT `je54-art01-commencement`
IMPORT `je54-art01-by-date`

-- je54-tests-art01-by-date: Article 1 asked with dates, on each of the three readings of fork I1.  Expected values were written from the text of Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of V1 and from the brief's description
-- of the three readings before this module was run.  The three readings are:
--   (a) `whether the enactment had come into force before 28 September 2021` (the default of the function; every test passes the reading explicitly),
--   (b) `the day the enactment was passed or made`,
--   (c) `the day on which the question about the enactment is asked`.
-- The days on which an enactment of 2003 to 2018 comes into force are read from the inferred text (Articles 1(5) and 1(6) are dated to 28 March 2003 by the endnotes of the 2019 consolidation; not verified against L.16/2003).
-- That the 2021 Law gives the same day for a named day was the brief's claim and is now checked.  Checked by the integrator on 2026-10-28: Article 3(2) of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 reads "it is treated as coming into force at the beginning of that day, unless provision is made to the contrary" (subject je/legislation-2021, source/l_8_2021.current.txt, line 48); it does not say whether a stated time of day is such a provision (fork L2 of that row).

GIVETH A `Which day selects the text for commencement`
`reading a` MEANS `whether the enactment had come into force before 28 September 2021`

GIVETH A `Which day selects the text for commencement`
`reading b` MEANS `the day the enactment was passed or made`

GIVETH A `Which day selects the text for commencement`
`reading c` MEANS `the day on which the question about the enactment is asked`

`the V1 basis` MEANS `read from the deposited text in force on that day`
`the inferred basis` MEANS `inferred from the endnotes of the 2019 consolidation, not verified against L.16/2003`
`the 2021 Law basis` MEANS `governed by the 2021 Law, Article 3(2)`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      mo IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
      h IS A NUMBER
      mi IS A NUMBER
      s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATETIME
`an instant in UTC` y mo d h mi s MEANS
    DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (YMD y mo d) (TIME_FROM_HMS h mi s) "Etc/UTC"

GIVEN named IS A DATE
      made IS A DATE
      asked IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Commencement as stated`
`an enactment that names the day` named `made on` made `asked about on` asked MEANS
    `Commencement as stated` WITH
        `how it is expressed` IS `on a particular day`
        `the day it names` IS JUST named
        `the day it was passed or made` IS made
        `the day the question is asked` IS asked

GIVEN made IS A DATE
      asked IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Commencement as stated`
`an enactment that is silent, made on` made `asked about on` asked MEANS
    `Commencement as stated` WITH
        `how it is expressed` IS `silent as to the time at which it is to come into operation`
        `the day it names` IS NOTHING
        `the day it was passed or made` IS made
        `the day the question is asked` IS asked

GIVEN made IS A DATE
      asked IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Commencement as stated`
`an enactment that says forthwith, made on` made `asked about on` asked MEANS
    `Commencement as stated` WITH
        `how it is expressed` IS `forthwith`
        `the day it names` IS NOTHING
        `the day it was passed or made` IS made
        `the day the question is asked` IS asked

GIVEN made IS A DATE
      asked IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Commencement as stated`
`an enactment that counts from its promulgation, made on` made `asked about on` asked MEANS
    `Commencement as stated` WITH
        `how it is expressed` IS `calculated by reference to its promulgation`
        `the day it names` IS NOTHING
        `the day it was passed or made` IS made
        `the day the question is asked` IS asked

GIVEN made IS A DATE
      asked IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Commencement as stated`
`an enactment that says a particular day but names none, made on` made `asked about on` asked MEANS
    `Commencement as stated` WITH
        `how it is expressed` IS `on a particular day`
        `the day it names` IS NOTHING
        `the day it was passed or made` IS made
        `the day the question is asked` IS asked


§ `A: made 20 September 2021 (before the 2021 Law), naming 1 October 2021 (after it)`

-- (a) the candidate day under V1 is 1 October 2021, which is after 27 September 2021: the 2021 Law governs.  (b) the text in force on 20 September 2021 is V1, which governs.  The day is the same; the governing provision differs.
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2021 10 1) `made on` (YMD 2021 9 20) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading a`)'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2021 10 1
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2021 10 1) `made on` (YMD 2021 9 20) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading a`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `the 2021 Law basis`
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2021 10 1) `made on` (YMD 2021 9 20) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading b`)'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2021 10 1
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2021 10 1) `made on` (YMD 2021 9 20) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading b`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `the V1 basis`
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2021 10 1) `made on` (YMD 2021 9 20) `asked about on` (JUST (YMD 2021 9 25))) `reading c`)'s `the day` EQUALS YMD 2021 10 1
#ASSERT (`Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2021 10 1) `made on` (YMD 2021 9 20) `asked about on` (JUST (YMD 2021 9 25))) `reading c`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `the V1 basis`
-- (c) asked on 28 October 2026: the text then in force is V2f, which has no Articles 1(5) and 1(6).
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2021 10 1) `made on` (YMD 2021 9 20) `asked about on` (JUST (YMD 2026 10 28))) `reading c`
        BECAUSE "from 28 September 2021 Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 are deleted (L.8/2021); the commencement of an enactment is then governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"

