§ `G: a time calculated from promulgation, a named day with no name, and no day given for reading (c)`

#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an enactment that counts from its promulgation, made on` (YMD 2020 6 10) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading a`
        BECAUSE "the time is calculated by reference to promulgation: Article 1(7) fixes the date of promulgation when it is unknown, but neither Law says how a period is counted from it, so no day is given"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an enactment that counts from its promulgation, made on` (YMD 2020 6 10) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading b`
        BECAUSE "the time is calculated by reference to promulgation: Article 1(7) fixes the date of promulgation when it is unknown, but neither Law says how a period is counted from it, so no day is given"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an enactment that says a particular day but names none, made on` (YMD 2020 6 10) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading a`
        BECAUSE "the enactment is said to come into operation on a particular day, but no day is named"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(5) and 1(6) by date: the day on which the enactment comes into force` (`an enactment that is silent, made on` (YMD 2020 6 10) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading c`
        BECAUSE "the reading chosen for Article 1 takes the text in force on the day the question is asked, and no such day has been given"

§ `The moment, in force on a day, in force at an instant`

-- Made 20 September 2021 naming 1 October 2021: 1 October 2021 00:00 in Jersey (BST, UTC+1) is 30 September 23:00 UTC.
#ASSERT DATETIME_SERIAL ((`Article 1(4) by date: the moment at which the enactment comes into force` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2021 10 1) `made on` (YMD 2021 9 20) `asked about on` NOTHING) "Europe/Jersey" `reading a`)'s `the moment`) EQUALS DATETIME_SERIAL (`an instant in UTC` 2021 9 30 23 0 0)
#ASSERT (`Article 1(4) by date: the moment at which the enactment comes into force` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2021 10 1) `made on` (YMD 2021 9 20) `asked about on` NOTHING) "Europe/Jersey" `reading a`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `the 2021 Law basis`
#ASSERT (`Article 1(4) by date: the moment at which the enactment comes into force` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2021 10 1) `made on` (YMD 2021 9 20) `asked about on` NOTHING) "Europe/Jersey" `reading b`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `the V1 basis`
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1(4) by date: the enactment is in force at the instant` (`an instant in UTC` 2021 9 30 22 59 59) "Europe/Jersey" (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2021 10 1) `made on` (YMD 2021 9 20) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading a`)'s `the answer`
#ASSERT (`Article 1(4) by date: the enactment is in force at the instant` (`an instant in UTC` 2021 9 30 23 0 0) "Europe/Jersey" (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2021 10 1) `made on` (YMD 2021 9 20) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading a`)'s `the answer`
#ASSERT (`Article 1(4) by date: the enactment is in force at the instant` (`an instant in UTC` 2021 9 30 23 0 0) "Europe/Jersey" (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2021 10 1) `made on` (YMD 2021 9 20) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading a`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `the 2021 Law basis`
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1(4) by date: the enactment is in force on the day` (YMD 2021 9 30) (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2021 10 1) `made on` (YMD 2021 9 20) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading a`)'s `the answer`
#ASSERT (`Article 1(4) by date: the enactment is in force on the day` (YMD 2021 10 1) (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2021 10 1) `made on` (YMD 2021 9 20) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading a`)'s `the answer`
#ASSERT (`Article 1(4) by date: the enactment is in force on the day` (YMD 2021 10 1) (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2021 10 1) `made on` (YMD 2021 9 20) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading b`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `the V1 basis`
-- Made 1 March 2020 naming 1 April 2020: 31 March 23:00 UTC is 1 April 00:00 in Jersey (BST, UTC+1); read on reading (a) the basis is the text of the day.
#ASSERT DATETIME_SERIAL ((`Article 1(4) by date: the moment at which the enactment comes into force` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2020 4 1) `made on` (YMD 2020 3 1) `asked about on` NOTHING) "Europe/Jersey" `reading a`)'s `the moment`) EQUALS DATETIME_SERIAL (`an instant in UTC` 2020 3 31 23 0 0)
#ASSERT (`Article 1(4) by date: the moment at which the enactment comes into force` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2020 4 1) `made on` (YMD 2020 3 1) `asked about on` NOTHING) "Europe/Jersey" `reading a`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `the V1 basis`
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 1(4) by date: the enactment is in force at the instant` (`an instant in UTC` 2020 3 31 22 59 59) "Europe/Jersey" (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2020 4 1) `made on` (YMD 2020 3 1) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading b`)'s `the answer`
#ASSERT (`Article 1(4) by date: the enactment is in force at the instant` (`an instant in UTC` 2020 3 31 23 0 0) "Europe/Jersey" (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2020 4 1) `made on` (YMD 2020 3 1) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading b`)'s `the answer`
-- Made in 2014: the moment is inferred, and the label says so.
#ASSERT (`Article 1(4) by date: the moment at which the enactment comes into force` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2014 11 21) `made on` (YMD 2014 11 21) `asked about on` NOTHING) "Europe/Jersey" `reading a`)'s `the basis` EQUALS `the inferred basis`
#ASSERT DATETIME_SERIAL ((`Article 1(4) by date: the moment at which the enactment comes into force` (`an enactment that names the day` (YMD 2014 11 21) `made on` (YMD 2014 11 21) `asked about on` NOTHING) "Europe/Jersey" `reading a`)'s `the moment`) EQUALS DATETIME_SERIAL (`an instant in UTC` 2014 11 21 0 0 0)
-- From 28 September 2021 every one of these refuses.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(4) by date: the moment at which the enactment comes into force` (`an enactment that is silent, made on` (YMD 2022 3 1) `asked about on` NOTHING) "Europe/Jersey" `reading a`
        BECAUSE "from 28 September 2021 Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 are deleted (L.8/2021); the commencement of an enactment is then governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(4) by date: the enactment is in force at the instant` (`an instant in UTC` 2022 3 1 12 0 0) "Europe/Jersey" (`an enactment that is silent, made on` (YMD 2022 3 1) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading b`
        BECAUSE "from 28 September 2021 Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 are deleted (L.8/2021); the commencement of an enactment is then governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(4) by date: the enactment is in force on the day` (YMD 2022 3 1) (`an enactment that is silent, made on` (YMD 2022 3 1) `asked about on` NOTHING) `reading a`
        BECAUSE "from 28 September 2021 Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 are deleted (L.8/2021); the commencement of an enactment is then governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"

§ `Article 1(7): the date of promulgation, by the day the enactment was passed or made`

-- Selecting date: the day the enactment was passed or made.  1 January 2019 is the first day with a deposited text; 31 December 2018 is the last day without.
#ASSERT `Article 1(7) by date: the date of promulgation to be used` TRUE (JUST (YMD 2019 12 1)) (YMD 2020 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2019 12 1
#ASSERT `Article 1(7) by date: the date of promulgation to be used` TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2020 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2020 1 1
#ASSERT `Article 1(7) by date: the date of promulgation to be used` TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2019 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2019 1 1
#ASSERT `Article 1(7) by date: the date of promulgation to be used` TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2026 10 28) EQUALS YMD 2026 10 28
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(7) by date: the date of promulgation to be used` TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2018 12 31)
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(7) by date: the date of promulgation to be used` FALSE NOTHING (YMD 2020 1 1)
        BECAUSE "Article 1(7) deals only with a time at which an enactment is to come into operation that is expressed or calculated by reference to its promulgation"

§ `Articles 1(1), 1(2) and 1(3) on a day: the text in force on the day the question is asked about`

#ASSERT `Article 1(1) on a day: the instrument is an enactment` (YMD 2019 1 1) `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 1(1) on a day: the instrument is an enactment` (YMD 2026 10 28) `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 1(1) on a day: the instrument is an enactment` (YMD 2026 10 28) `something that is none of these` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(1) on a day: the instrument is an enactment` (YMD 2018 12 31) `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` FALSE
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"

-- 1(2) is in V1 only: confirmed 10 May 2020, registered 20 May 2020; the later day is 20 May 2020.
#ASSERT `Article 1(2) on a day: the day on which a Law is deemed passed` (YMD 2020 6 1) (YMD 2020 5 10) (YMD 2020 5 20) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS YMD 2020 5 20
#ASSERT `Article 1(2) on a day: the day on which a Law is deemed passed` (YMD 2021 9 27) (YMD 2020 5 20) (YMD 2020 5 10) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS YMD 2020 5 20
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(2) on a day: the day on which a Law is deemed passed` (YMD 2021 9 28) (YMD 2020 5 10) (YMD 2020 5 20) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` NOTHING FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 1(2) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not among the provisions answered before 1 January 2019"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(2) on a day: the day on which a Law is deemed passed` (YMD 2018 12 31) (YMD 2020 5 10) (YMD 2020 5 20) `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` NOTHING FALSE
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"

#ASSERT `Article 1(3) on a day: how a reference to passing or repeal is read` (YMD 2019 1 1) `passing` TRUE EQUALS `as a reference to the making of the enactment`
#ASSERT `Article 1(3) on a day: how a reference to passing or repeal is read` (YMD 2026 10 28) `repeal` TRUE EQUALS `as a reference to the rescission of the enactment`
#ASSERT `Article 1(3) on a day: how a reference to passing or repeal is read` (YMD 2026 10 28) `repeal` FALSE EQUALS `as written`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1(3) on a day: how a reference to passing or repeal is read` (YMD 2018 12 31) `passing` TRUE
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"

